Where the Project is or includes works to a HRB, the Consultant shall: 
{br}{br}7.6.1 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; establish and maintain a Mandatory Occurrence Reporting System and Mandatory Occurrence Reporting Plan in accordance with the Building Safety Legislation;
{br}{br}7.6.2 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; take reasonable steps to ensure each Reporting Person is provided with adequate instruction and information on the Mandatory Occurrence Reporting System and the incidents or situations that should be reported by the Reporting Person through the Mandatory Occurrence Reporting System:
{br}{br}&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(a) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; in the case of a designer or contractor, before beginning any work in relation to the Project; and
{br}{br}&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(b) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; in the case of any other person, as soon as reasonably practicable after first entering the site of the Project; and{br}{br}
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(c) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; in accordance with the Building Safety Legislation ensure an appropriate frequency of inspections of the Project for Safety Occurrences;
{br}{br}&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(d) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; liaise and co-operate with each other to ensure that each Safety Occurrence is notified and reported to the Building Safety Regulator in accordance with the Building Safety Legislation; and
{br}{br}&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(e) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; for each Safety Occurrence, consider whether a Controlled Change is necessary to remedy the Safety Occurrence. If a Controlled Change is required, the Consultant shall either:
{br}{br}&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(i) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;make a Change Control Application or notify, as applicable, the Building Safety Regulator; or
{br}{br}&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;(ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;liaise, as appropriate, with the Building Regulations Principal Contractor to make such Change Control Application or otherwise notify the Building Safety Regulator under the terms of its Building Contract;
{br}{br}7.6.3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;when requested by the Contractor to do so, the Consultant shall promptly provide the Mandatory Occurrence Reporting Plan.
